@chat Motion Lab
@subtitle Animated scripted messages: animate(), tween(), transition(), ease.*
@icon sparkles
@participant me | You | #007aff | me
@participant mo | Mo | #ff9f0a

--- mo 14:00
litehtml has no CSS transitions, transforms or opacity, so every moving value here is a script re-rendering its message up to <b>60 times a second</b>, driven by <code>animate()</code> and <code>tween()</code> with the <code>ease.*</code> curves. Each frame changes ordinary properties: sizes, margins, absolute positions, rgba colours (<code>mix()</code>, <code>alpha()</code>), gradient angles, or a freshly generated SVG image. When a card swaps whole content (a tab, a step, a result), <code>transition('slide-left')</code> or <code>'pop'</code> lets the bubble animate it natively. Animation pauses whenever a card is off screen, and every loop stops once nothing moves.

